"BILINEARITY TEST:" println
"  If algorithm works for:" println
"    (A+A')×B = A×B + A'×B (linear in first argument)" println
"    A×(B+B') = A×B + A×B' (linear in second argument)" println
"  Then we can verify with far fewer test cases!" println
"" println

"POLYNOMIAL IDENTITY:" println
"  Matrix multiplication is polynomial in entries" println
"  Only need to test with ~20 random matrices" println
"  Probability of false positive: < 10^-20" println
"  (Schwartz-Zippel lemma)" println
"" println

"RANK LOWER BOUND:" println
"  Tensor rank ≥ certain algebraic bounds" println
"  For 3×3: proven that rank ≥ 19" println
"  So we don't waste time searching for <19 multiplications" println
"" println

"SYMMETRY:" println
"  Can assume certain orderings without loss of generality" println
"  Reduces search by factor of n! (factorial)" println
"" println

