"═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════" println
"STRASSEN'S ALGORITHM (REFERENCE)" println
"═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════" println
"" println

"For 2×2 matrices A=[[a,b],[c,d]], B=[[e,f],[g,h]]:" println
"" println

"M1 = (a + d) × (e + h)" println
"M2 = (c + d) × e" println
"M3 = a × (f - h)" println
"M4 = d × (g - e)" println
"M5 = (a + b) × h" println
"M6 = (c - a) × (e + f)" println
"M7 = (b - d) × (g + h)" println
"" println

"Result:" println
"C00 = M1 + M4 - M5 + M7" println
"C01 = M3 + M5" println
"C10 = M2 + M4" println
"C11 = M1 - M2 + M3 + M6" println
"" println

"Notice the structure:" println
"  - Each M_i uses 2-3 elements from A and B" println
"  - Coefficients are {-1, 0, 1}" println
"  - Symmetric patterns: (a+b), (a-b)" println
"  - Final combinations use {-1, 1}" println
"" println

"This structure guides our search!" println
